      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1961, New Square became incorporated as a village after a New York state court ruled in its favor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Square%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The predominant language spoken in New Square, New York, is Yiddish, reflecting its Hasidic community's culture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Square%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Construction of New Square began in 1956, with the first families moving in by December of that year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Square%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "New Square's founders initially intended to name the settlement New Skvir, but a typist's error changed it to New Square.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
